fy an ID that is unique to the entire document. This attribute group is not used for a required id attribute, or for an id attribute that specifies an id reference."}]}]},{"name":"figure","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The individual figures, ordered from top to bottom."}]}]},{"name":"duration","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The duration element is defined within a group due to its uses within the note, figured-bass, backup, and forward elements."}]}]},{"name":"footnote","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The footnote element specifies editorial information that appears in footnotes in the printed score. It is defined within a group due to its multiple uses within the MusicXML schema."}]}]},{"name":"level","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The level element specifies editorial information for different MusicXML elements. It is defined within a group due to its multiple uses within the MusicXML schema."}]}]},{"name":"position","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be changed two ways."}]}]},{"name":"font","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The font attribute group gathers together attributes for determining the font within a credit or direction. They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of font names.The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text font vs. a music font."}]}]},{"name":"color","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element."}]}]},{"name":"halign","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In cases where text extends over more than one line, horizontal alignment and justify values can be different. The most typical case is for credits, such as:"}]}]},{"name":"valign","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The valign attribute is used to indicate vertical alignment to the top, middle, bottom, or baseline of the text. Defaults are implementation-dependent."}]}]},{"name":"placement","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The placement attribute indicates whether something is above or below another element, such as a note or a notation."}]}]},{"name":"printout","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The printout attribute group collects the different controls over printing an object (e.g. a note or rest) and its parts, including augmentation dots and lyrics. This is especially useful for notes that overlap in different voices, or for chord sheets that contain lyrics and chords but no melody."}]}]},{"name":"hasParentheses","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A Boolean value indicating whether the figures are enclosed in parentheses. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"type":"text","text":" if not specified."}]}]}],"kind":"parameters"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlfiguredbass\/init(id:figure:duration:footnote:level:position:font:color:halign:valign:placement:printout:hasparentheses:)"]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFiguredBass\/init(id:figure:duration:footnote:level:position:font:color:halign:valign:placement:printout:hasParentheses:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLFiguredBassV2id6figure8duration8footnote5level8position4font5color6halign6valign9placement8printout14